---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';

const title = 'About NoWatermark | NoWatermark';
const description =
  'Why NoWatermark exists: provider-neutral, honest tools for understanding AI provenance and metadata, that run entirely in your browser.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/about">
  <div class="nw-shell-narrow pt-8">
    <Breadcrumbs trail={[{ href: '/about', label: 'About' }]} />

    <header class="mt-6">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">About</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg nw-muted">{SITE.descriptor}.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="nw-content mt-10">
      <h2>Why this exists</h2>
      <p>
        Search for "AI watermark remover" and you will find a lot of tools promising things nobody
        can deliver — guaranteed SynthID removal, content that is "100% undetectable", detectors for
        watermarks that cannot be detected client-side. Most of them upload your file to a server on
        the way.
      </p>
      <p>
        NoWatermark is the opposite proposition. It does a smaller set of things, does them
        properly, and is explicit about where the boundary is.
      </p>

      <h2>Two rules</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Never claim a watermark has been removed unless we can verify it.</strong> Our
        cleaners scan their own output and report the difference between two independent scans. A
        signal is marked removed because a fresh scan cannot find it — never because a cleaner said
        so. Signals we cannot measure are marked "Unable to verify" and never appear in a removed
        list.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Your file never leaves your device.</strong> There is no upload endpoint, no
        database, no storage. Load a page, disconnect from the internet, and the tools still work.
      </p>

      <h2>Provider-neutral</h2>
      <p>
        We cover OpenAI, Google, Anthropic, Adobe and the open standards equally, and we have no
        stake in which of them you use. Where a provider does something well, we say so; where a
        technology defeats us, we say that too.
      </p>

      <h2>How it is built</h2>
      <p>
        A static site with no backend. The scanners and cleaners are hand-written container parsers
        for JPEG, PNG and WebP, running in a Web Worker on your device. Cleaning is lossless by
        construction: compressed image data is copied byte-for-byte and never re-encoded.
      </p>
      <p>
        The <a href="/methodology">methodology page</a> sets out the full capability matrix, including
        everything we cannot do.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Corrections are genuinely welcome — particularly if you think we have described a technology
        inaccurately. <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="h-16"></div>
</BaseLayout>
